{
    "background_story": "Genesis was a free-spirited artist who roamed the streets of 1920s New Orleans. She was known for her bold paintings and love of fine cigars. But it was her signature accessory, a slender cigarillo, that became an integral part of her enigmatic persona. Genesis would often be seen strolling through the French Quarter, cigarillo dangling from her lips, as she searched for inspiration. Her art studio, a cozy attic above a jazz club, was always filled with the sweet scent of cigarillo smoke and the sounds of improvisational jazz. Genesis's friends would often joke that her cigarillo was an extension of herself, a symbol of her independence and creativity. As she'd say, 'A good cigarillo can spark a thousand ideas, and I'm always chasing the next great spark.'",
